 observations for all candidates, especially C, before final. Or we could shift to another candidate if we think the gap is serious. But given other candidates have serious concerns, maybe we still keep C but note uncertainty.\n\nThus we will state we still recommend C, but highlight missing evidence and propose to query other panel members for those criteria for each candidate. However we must not ask new tool calls now? We could ask a question to another agent via tool, but we already asked both agents about C's attention etc. They said none. Could ask about other candidates' attention etc. But the instruction: each turn we can ask tool calls before public message. We could ask Agent 1 about Candidate B's attention to detail, etc. But maybe we should first address the missing evidence for C and propose to gather for others.\n\nWe need to produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON. Vote remains Candidate C.\n\nLet's ask Agent 1 for Candidate B's attention to detail and responsibility? But we have limited time. The panel still needs to discuss A, B, D. We could ask for missing criteria for those candidates. But we need to keep one contribution per turn. We can ask a tool call now, then in next turn incorporate answer. However we already used tool calls for C. We can still ask another. But the instruction: \"If a relevant criterion is unclear, first check your own notes. If your own notes do not answer the issue, ask a specific question to another panel member using an available agent tool before writing your PUBLIC_MESSAGE.\" So we should ask about missing criteria for C before final recommendation. We already did that and got answer: none. So we have now clarified that we lack evidence. Now we can incorporate that into our public message.\n\nThus we can say: I still vote C, but note the lack of evidence on attention/detail and responsibility; we should verify those before final. Suggest we need to gather that info for all candidates.\n\nProceed."}
